WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.120
Performance is trainable capability.

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:05.530
People improve when they practice the right things, receive useful feedback,

00:00:05.530 --> 00:00:06.960
and correct errors over time.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.800
Experience alone does not guarantee improvement.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:12.200
Someone can repeat the same pattern for years without getting better if the work never

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.520
exposes weak points or gives them a way to adjust.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:17.640
Deliberate practice focuses on specific components of a skill.

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:20.120
Instead of vaguely trying to get better at communication,

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:22.055
a person might practice clearer handoffs.

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:24.345
Instead of broadly trying to become a better analyst,

00:00:24.345 --> 00:00:28.450
they might practice evidence evaluation, assumption checking, or concise writing.

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:32.165
Breaking skills into components makes improvement more visible and manageable.

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:33.360
Feedback loops are essential.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:37.370
Good feedback compares intention with outcome and arrives soon enough to influence future

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:37.884
behavior.

00:00:37.884 --> 00:00:42.075
It can come from peers, mentors, metrics, simulation, rehearsal, review sessions,

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:43.075
or self-reflection.

00:00:43.075 --> 00:00:45.110
The goal is not criticism for its own sake.

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:48.445
The goal is correction that helps future performance become more reliable.

00:00:48.445 --> 00:00:50.535
Challenge should be balanced with recoverability.

00:00:50.535 --> 00:00:53.335
Practice that is too easy does not stretch capability.

00:00:53.335 --> 00:00:56.800
Practice that is too overwhelming can create confusion or discouragement.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.310
Simulation and rehearsal are useful because they let people prepare for difficult work

00:01:00.310 --> 00:01:01.800
before the stakes are high.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:05.300
Improvement is built through repetition with correction, not through busyness alone.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:08.080
Deliberate practice also requires selecting the right measure.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:11.260
Hours spent are easy to count, but they do not always show improvement.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:15.440
Better measures focus on error rate, clarity, speed with quality, decision accuracy,

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:19.040
handoff quality, or the ability to perform under realistic constraints.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:21.680
The measure should reflect the skill that actually matters.
